<item><title>MRC asks Cameroon officials to clear election-candidate paperwork</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/mrc-asks-cameroon-officials-to-clear-election-candidate-207424/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/mrc-asks-cameroon-officials-to-clear-election-candidate-207424/</guid><category>Cameroon</category><description>The opposition party says thousands of its members face delays, refusals or demands for payment as they prepare for the 7 February 2027 vote.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 08:54:20 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/mrc-asks-cameroon-officials-to-clear-election-candidate-207424/share.jpg" length="41092" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/mrc-asks-cameroon-officials-to-clear-election-candidate-207424/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Cameroon allocates CFAF 550 million to 30 student businesses and 50 incubators</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-allocates-cfaf-550-million-to-30-student-36fd74/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-allocates-cfaf-550-million-to-30-student-36fd74/</guid><category>Cameroon</category><description>Of the 2026 grants, CFAF 350 million goes to ventures at higher education institutions, and nearly two-thirds of student funding backs food processing and agro-industry.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:56:38 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" length="34085" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>COSUMAF reports Cameroon’s fund-investment share at 3.463%</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cosumaf-reports-cameroon-s-fund-investment-share-at-3-463-be5ce9/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cosumaf-reports-cameroon-s-fund-investment-share-at-3-463-be5ce9/</guid><category>Cameroon</category><description>The regulator’s June figure is down from 20.8% in February, but its reports contain inconsistencies and do not establish that funds sold Cameroonian debt.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:59:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" length="34085" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Aeternum signs $1.91 million in funding deals for Cameroon project developer</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/aeternum-signs-1-91-million-in-funding-deals-for-cameroon-5ede31/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/aeternum-signs-1-91-million-in-funding-deals-for-cameroon-5ede31/</guid><category>Cameroon</category><description>The eight agreements relate to its planned acquisition of American Renaissance Minerals, which is involved in the Nkamouna project in eastern Cameroon.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:41:48 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" length="34085" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Cameroonian engineer builds solar-powered clay cooler</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroonian-engineer-builds-solar-powered-clay-cooler-11a8d2/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroonian-engineer-builds-solar-powered-clay-cooler-11a8d2/</guid><category>Cameroon</category><description>Didier Dinamou’s prototype uses porous clay, water and a photovoltaic panel, and its designer says it can cool a room to 25 degrees in 48-degree heat.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:05:28 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" length="34085" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
